  "final_message": "**Status: reproduced.** The bug happens on this checkout (a9269c6). I didn't change any production code.\n\n**Command** (from the repo root):\n\n```\nnpx vitest run --project unit packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotNames.spec.ts\n```\n\nIt exits 1 while the bug is present and should exit 0 once it's fixed. The check is the new file `packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotNames.spec.ts`, which is the only change in the working tree.\n\n**What I saw:** 1 test failed and 1 passed.\n\n- The failing test uses the report's `App.vue` structure. `<BaseLayout>` has a conditional `<template v-if=... #randomslotname>`, and a sibling `<SubComponent>` is given `<template #title>` and `<template #_duration>`.\n- The rendered output was:\n  `<div><p class=\"conditional\">conditional slot</p><div class=\"given-title\">given title</div><div class=\"default-duration\">default _duration</div></div>`\n- `#title` renders the supplied content, but `#_duration` falls back to its default slot content. That matches the report: \"The default slot content is being rendered and not replaced with the template content.\"\n\n**It passes where it should:**\n\n- **Without the trigger:** the second test in the same file has the same markup without the `v-if` sibling template. It passes, and both slots render the supplied content.\n- **Last good version:** I installed published `vue@3.5.13` and `vue@3.5.14` in a scratch directory and rendered the same template with each, using jsdom. 3.5.13 renders `given-duration` (exit 0). 3.5.14 renders `default-duration` (exit 1). This matches the report's \"works in 3.5.13, broken since 3.5.14\".\n\nThe test uses the runtime template compiler (`components` option and `template` string) rather than SFC and `<script setup>`. The failure is the same as in the report's playground project, which I decoded from the link.\n",
  "run_command": "npx vitest run --project unit packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotNames.spec.ts",
  "patch": "diff --git a/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotNames.spec.ts b/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotNames.spec.ts\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..1660967\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotNames.spec.ts\n@@ -0,0 +1,80 @@\n+import { createApp } from '../src'\n+\n+// Reproduction for: \"Slot <template> not working when its name starts with an\n+// underscore (_) since v3.5.14\".\n+//\n+// App -> BaseLayout (has a conditionally rendered slot template `v-if`) and a\n+// sibling SubComponent whose slots are provided with `<template #title>` and\n+// `<template #_duration>`.\n+describe('slot names starting with an underscore (reported bug)', () => {\n+  const SubComponent = {\n+    template: `\n+      <slot name=\"title\"><div class=\"default-title\">default title</div></slot>\n+      <slot name=\"_duration\"><div class=\"default-duration\">default _duration</div></slot>\n+    `,\n+  }\n+\n+  const BaseLayout = {\n+    template: `\n+      <div>\n+        <slot name=\"randomslotname\"></slot>\n+        <slot></slot>\n+      </div>\n+    `,\n+  }\n+\n+  function render(appTemplate: string) {\n+    const container = document.createElement('div')\n+    createApp({\n+      components: { SubComponent, BaseLayout },\n+      data: () => ({ anyConditionCheckHereWillDo: true }),\n+      template: appTemplate,\n+    }).mount(container)\n+    return container.innerHTML\n+  }\n+\n+  // exactly the structure of the report's App.vue\n+  it('renders `#_duration` slot content when sibling of a v-if slot template', () => {\n+    const html = render(`\n+      <BaseLayout>\n+        <template v-if=\"anyConditionCheckHereWillDo\" #randomslotname>\n+          <p class=\"conditional\">conditional slot</p>\n+        </template>\n+\n+        <SubComponent>\n+          <template #title>\n+            <div class=\"given-title\">given title</div>\n+          </template>\n+          <template #_duration>\n+            <div class=\"given-duration\">given _duration</div>\n+          </template>\n+        </SubComponent>\n+      </BaseLayout>\n+    `)\n+    // non-underscore slot works\n+    expect(html).toContain('given-title')\n+    expect(html).not.toContain('default-title')\n+    // underscore slot is expected to work too (it did in 3.5.13)\n+    expect(html).toContain('given-duration')\n+    expect(html).not.toContain('default-duration')\n+  })\n+\n+  // same thing without the conditional sibling template: works\n+  it('control: renders `#_duration` slot content without the v-if sibling', () => {\n+    const html = render(`\n+      <BaseLayout>\n+        <SubComponent>\n+          <template #title>\n+            <div class=\"given-title\">given title</div>\n+          </template>\n+          <template #_duration>\n+            <div class=\"given-duration\">given _duration</div>\n+          </template>\n+        </SubComponent>\n+      </BaseLayout>\n+    `)\n+    expect(html).toContain('given-title')\n+    expect(html).toContain('given-duration')\n+    expect(html).not.toContain('default-duration')\n+  })\n+})\n"
}
